.DS_Store
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.envrc
.direnv
**/build
*.log
*.mmon
/build/
/env.sh
/out.wav
/mods.csv
/renders/
.superpowers/
.worktrees/

# Local agent index -- a map of this working copy, not project documentation.
/CLAUDE.md
/.claude/

# Windows shell droppings -- the .DS_Store of this machine.
Thumbs.db
ehthumbs.db
desktop.ini

# Editor and tooling local state. compile_commands.json is emitted into
# build/ by CMake; the root copy is only ever a convenience symlink for
# clangd, and CMakeUserPresets.json is per-developer by CMake's own
# convention (CMakePresets.json is the tracked one).
.vs/
.cache/
/compile_commands.json
/CMakeUserPresets.json

# Object and dependency files. Both toolchains write these into their own
# build dirs, so a stray one at any other path is an accident.
*.o
*.d
*.obj

# Sampler source material for the render-host scenarios. Two kinds live here,
# neither belongs in the repo: the user's own sample library (large, and not
# ours to redistribute), and material bounced from Spotykach itself by
# scenarios like assets_percussive_source.json, which is regenerable. A
# scenario referencing a missing input fails loudly, which is the right
# behaviour -- it is not silently rendered as silence.
# Generator scripts (e.g. gen_clicks.py) are code, not sample material --
# tracked so the material they write is reproducible from a clean checkout.
/host/render/scenarios/assets/*
!/host/render/scenarios/assets/*.py
